  "body": "Slice 1 of #661: the SVG-to-PNG icon pipeline and the operation icons (checklist sections 1-3). Every `OpType` now has its own icon.\n\n## What changed\n- **Pipeline (`cargo xtask icons`, new `xtask/src/icons.rs`).** Each icon has an SVG master in `assets/ui/svg/*.svg`. The command rasterises it to the 32x32 PNG the UI already embeds (`assets/ui/<stem>.png`), and the PNGs are committed. `--check` re-renders every master and fails when a committed PNG differs from it (more than 8 per channel) or when a master breaks the house rules. `--sheet <out.png> [--px 16] [--zoom 4]` draws a contact sheet on a dark band and a light band so a person can look at the set. Rendering uses `resvg =0.45.1` (MIT OR Apache-2.0) with default features off. It is an **xtask-only** dependency: nothing new at runtime in the app or ui crates, and no `build.rs`. It reuses the lock's existing `tiny-skia 0.11`.\n- **House rules (enforced by the lint):** Tabler conventions (`viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\"`, no intrinsic size, round caps and joins, stroke 2 for the object and 1.5 for a toolpath/detail line), `currentColor` ink, shapes only (no image, script, text, style, href, `url(` or font). The loader still sets every pixel to white and lets alpha draw, so one PNG works in both themes.\n- **41 original operation icons** (22 new, 5 stand-ins redrawn, 13 earlier originals redrawn, plus Trochoidal Slot and Plasma Profile, which are in the enum now). Each is drawn from what the operation does: a cutter and its path. Each family shares a frame: 2D in plan or section; multi-axis on a dome with the ball leaning on its normal; rotary on a bar with the tool riding the radial; every turning kind with a solid chuck block on the left.\n- **Wiring.** `icons.rs` is now one macro table that generates the enum, `ALL`, the bytes and the texture keys (195 lines). `op_icon` moved out of the oversized `panes.rs` into a new `op_icons.rs` and maps every kind to its own slot; the old reuse law is retired. The turning section door now uses the Facing icon. Face is drawn in plan view, Facing in side view. The 18 PNGs nothing uses any more (13 earlier originals and 5 Tabler stand-ins) are deleted. `assets/ui/LICENSES.md` is updated: the op icons and their masters are ours, and the Tabler list excludes them.\n- `.claude/PROCESS_VERSION` -> 24 (main reads 23 after #1100) (`xtask/` is a process file). Fork note for #681: no action beyond the normal process sync; the new `icons` task needs `resvg` in the lock, which the synced `xtask/Cargo.toml` brings in.\n\n## Icons by source\n| Drawn original | Tabler |\n|---|---|\n| all 41 `op-*` icons (face, contour, pocket, adaptive2d, offset2d, slot, trochoidal-slot, trace, engrave, chamfer2d, deburr, circular, plasma-profile, drill, bore, thread, probe, pocket3d, finish3d, contour5d, parallel5d, swarf, advanced-swarf, rotary-contour, rotary-parallel, rotary-offset, multiaxis-rough, flow5d, multiaxis-contour, facing, profile-rough, profile-finish, groove-rough, groove-finish, part-off, threading, chamfering, taper-turning, multipass-turning, form-turning, boring-turning) | none new (the chrome icons are unchanged) |\n\nNothing comes from HSMWorks, Fusion or SolidCraft. SolidCraft's interface material has been under its own brand licence since upstream 312454f899 (recorded in the decision).\n\n## Merged main (2026-11-12, about 55 merges)\n- `.claude/PROCESS_VERSION`: conflict; now 24.\n- `crates/ui/src/egui_app/tests/structural.rs`: conflict. Kept main's new `ribbon_labels_whole_and_captions_painted` (#948). Main's version brings the file to 398 lines, so my `every_op_kind_has_its_own_svg_mastered_icon` moved, unchanged, into a new `tests/op_icon_table.rs`.\n- `Cargo.lock`, `xtask/` (#965/#967 gate rework), `panes.rs`, `icons.rs`, `mod.rs`: merged without conflicts. `Cargo.lock` adds only `resvg` and its dependencies; existing entries changed only by gaining version suffixes (`png 0.18.1`, `kurbo 0.13.1`, `base64 0.13.1`), with no version moved. `OpType` on main has the same 41 kinds, so nothing new needed carrying into `op_icons.rs`.\n\n## Decision\n`docs/decisions/661-icon-set.md` covers the pipeline, the dependency, the house rules, the SolidCraft licence finding, and what was considered and dropped.\n\n## How tested (pinning tests)\n- xtask: `committed_icon_pngs_match_their_svg_masters` (every committed PNG matches a fresh render of its master), `lint_accepts_a_clean_master`, `lint_refuses_raster_scripts_text_and_external_refs`, `lint_refuses_off_grid_sizes_caps_and_weights`, `render_draws_ink_on_the_32_px_grid`. `cargo test -p xtask`: 38 passed.\n- ui structural (`tests/op_icon_table.rs`): `every_op_kind_has_its_own_svg_mastered_icon` checks that every `KindInfo::ALL` kind maps to its own `op-*` icon with an SVG master, and that no two slots share a PNG.\n- `cargo test -p camcraft-ui` (all suites, CWD `crates/ui`): green, lib 532 passed. `cargo clippy -p xtask -p camcraft-ui --all-targets -D warnings`: clean. `cargo xtask icons --check`: 0 breaches.\n- `cargo xtask gate quick --base origin/main` falls back to **batch** because of the `Cargo.lock` change. The batch steps I did not run are the geometry/cl/tools/post/sim/motion/app suites. Their crates are untouched, and `resvg` only enters xtask's graph.\n- Looked at: every icon at 32 px and the whole set at 16 px on dark and light (`cargo xtask icons --sheet sheet.png --px 16 --zoom 4`, and `--px 32 --zoom 2`).\n\n## Least happy with\n- **Thread milling**: the sawtooth hole walls are busy at 16 px.\n- **Advanced Swarf**: a curved blade with the tool at two poses reads as \"two tools\" more than as \"swarf, advanced\".\n- (Redrawn after review: Face is now a plan view with a serpentine raster, so it no longer echoes Facing; Groove Rough is the plunge comb with the blade lifted and Groove Finish the bare U finishing path, which now read apart at 16 px.)\n- **5-axis Contour**: the ring arcs crowd the dome at 16 px.\n- **Deburr**: a small ball on a broken corner; it is the subtlest icon in the set.\n\n## Not exercised\nNot seen in the running app (no GUI launch): the toolbar, tree rows and operation pages with the new textures.\n\n## Snapshots\nNo file under `crates/ui/tests/snapshots/` is changed. The toolbar and tree icons will render differently in the release-lane pixel goldens (`egui_app*.png`), so those need the normal refresh at the next cut.\n\n## Still owed on #661\nSection 4 (tool types), 6 (tree rows), 7 (status badges), 8 (actions); section 5 (tabs) lands with #659.\n\nEffort: high (not escalated)\n\nChangelog: Every operation kind has its own original icon in the toolbar and the tree (turning, holes, 3D, multi-axis, 2D); icons are now SVG masters rasterised by `cargo xtask icons`. (#661)\n\nRefs #661\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\n\n",
